Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Fetches are made with fae magic, but they are not themselves fae, they're animated by a piece of human soul stuck inside them, and their unnatural powers only manifest as a result of their changeling double being out in the world somewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wyrd powers turn off when touched with cold iron. </div> </div> </div>Also no. Iron is an insurmountable obstacle to fae magic and inimical to the Gentry. This is not the same thing as being &quot;fairy antimagic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What would happen to a Fetch? I imagine placing it on the Fetch wouldn't do much, but what if it's implanted? </div> </div> </div>Still nothing. A fetch is utterly unremarkable until the rest of the soul-fragment it holds gets home except for maybe if it's assembled with a catch or dies in the right (or wrong) fashion.<br /> <br /> This is the thing the Others threw together to sicken and die in your place, and notwithstanding a couple missed details it's built to function like a mortal human for as long as there's need for a mortal human. It would be kind of a shitty replica if it dropped the pretense or fell apart from touching the wrong fence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/ava